ts complete projections, and then materializes every transcript message (`E:\\Projects\\Code\\AI\\Ji\\ji-java\\core\\ji-session-api\\src\\main\\java\\io\\github\\diodeme\\ji\\session\\tree\\SessionDocument.java:65-78,1001-1003,1646-1712`). Only afterward does `timeline` select the requested window, whose REST default is 50 (`E:\\Projects\\Code\\AI\\Ji\\ji-java\\applications\\ji-host-web\\src\\main\\java\\io\\github\\diodeme\\ji\\host\\web\\LocalHostServer.java:269-285`). Because Java intrinsic synchronization covers the whole `MemoryHostStore` instance, this work blocks operations across all sessions in that store. This is realistic for Stage 4 embedded/custom deployments: the architecture explicitly supports memory and custom stores (`E:\\Projects\\Code\\AI\\Ji\\docs\\java-rewrite\\02-target-architecture.md:67-76`), while Stage 4 includes the cursor timeline (`E:\\Projects\\Code\\AI\\Ji\\docs\\java-rewrite\\10-roadmap-and-risks.md:142-150`). The default standalone CLI’s SQLite path is unaffected because it uses an indexed `ORDER BY … LIMIT limit+1` query."}]